Subject: [PATCH] platform/x86: oxpec: release ACPI global lock after EC read errors

The preserved oxpec.upstream.c from the named Valve-tag mirror returns directly
when ec_read() fails, bypassing the acquired ACPI global lock's release. Battery
extension registration/uevents and ordinary hwmon reads can reach this path; a
read-only module trial can therefore leave the global lock held. Module exit
contains no corresponding recovery.

Route every acquired read-helper path through the existing unlock operation,
return the original ec_read status after a successful release, and initialize
that status to retain zero-length read behavior. Acquisition failure still
returns without release, and release failure retains the existing -EBUSY result.
The write helper already attempts release after ec_write success or failure and
is unchanged. This patch is separate from the seven-line OXP3 DMI mapping; the
preserved mirror source is unchanged. No EC register/value policy is changed.

--- a/oxpec.c
+++ b/oxpec.c
@@ -310,7 +310,7 @@
 static int read_from_ec(u8 reg, int size, long *val)
 {
 	u8 buffer;
-	int ret;
+	int ret = 0;
 	int i;
 
 	if (!lock_global_acpi_lock())
@@ -320,15 +320,16 @@
 	for (i = 0; i < size; i++) {
 		ret = ec_read(reg + i, &buffer);
 		if (ret)
-			return ret;
+			goto out_unlock;
 		*val <<= i * 8;
 		*val += buffer;
 	}
 
+out_unlock:
 	if (!unlock_global_acpi_lock())
 		return -EBUSY;
 
-	return 0;
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static int write_to_ec(u8 reg, u8 value)
